<title>HONG KONG: SIA receives fifth Boeing 747-400F.</title>
<headline>SIA receives fifth Boeing 747-400F.</headline>
<byline>Jim Gilchrist</byline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Airlines Ltd (SIA) has taken delivery of a new Boeing 747-400 freighter, an airline spokesman has told Reuters.</p>
<p>The new arrival brings SIA's cargo fleet to five 747-400 and one 747-200 freighter which is expected to be replaced by a sixth 747-400 in March next year, the spokesman added.</p>
<p>SIA's latest 747 freighter flew into Singapore's Changi airport on November 27 and is due to make its first revenue earning flight to San Francisco and Los Angeles at a date yet to be announced.</p>
<p>It will then be used on all SIA's cargo routes worldwide, the spokesman added. --Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 8982 Fax +44 171 542 5017</p>
